WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.887
One honest slide about what the
overview made look simpler than it is.

2
00:00:03.887 --> 00:00:05.501
This is design guidance.

3
00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:08.288
First, a mover reaches more than groups.

4
00:00:08.288 --> 00:00:12.637
Access that came from a package or a
direct assignment doesn't leave when a

5
00:00:12.637 --> 00:00:16.987
rule stops matching, and losing a licensed
group can take a mailbox with it.

6
00:00:16.987 --> 00:00:19.863
That's why the review of
what's left is a control.

7
00:00:19.863 --> 00:00:22.725
Second, hybrid lasts longer than planned.

8
00:00:22.725 --> 00:00:27.801
Retiring AD means clearing named
dependencies, and the end state may be a dated

9
00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:33.112
Kerberos island, a program decision made
at the start and revisited after rollout.

10
00:00:33.112 --> 00:00:36.924
An island with no end date goes
to the authorizing official.

11
00:00:36.924 --> 00:00:39.287
Third, the numbers are proposals.

12
00:00:39.287 --> 00:00:44.001
Ninety-nine percent correlation is a
starting point, not a federal requirement.

13
00:00:44.001 --> 00:00:47.350
Treat every threshold as
a decision with an owner.
